tags: udp

A transport layer: UDP, as RFC 768 specifies. Each address gives one IP address and one
port. Each message is one datagram.

The port is not a part of the protocol: each node selects its own port, and the address
gives it. A layer above UDP selects nothing in it: the port selects the protocol.

A layer has no value. A reader that does not know the layer does not call the address
on it.

